      "content": "You raise a critical point that highlights the extreme uncertainty in designing global wealth taxes without current levels of international cooperation. It is fair to argue that acting on this policy with such limitedCoordination carries a high risk of backfiring, as seen in cases like France where capital flight outweighed revenue gains in the short term. Many economists now recommend focusing on more immediate and domestically enforceable methods—such as higher capital gains taxes or progressive income taxation—to mitigate inequality while waiting for clearer paths to global alignment.",
